            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Winter celebrants beware! A song at the door may herald the arrival of a mari lwyd, a shrouded creature with a grinning, horse-like skull. Despite their macabre visage, these fey singers mean no harm, wishing only to join in with seasonal festivities and partake in hospitality. They're especially partial to alcohol and cheese but can be appeased with other treats if the household has none.</p>",
